# supabase/.env
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Edge Function secrets for E-CYAMUNARA
# 
# HOW TO SET THESE IN SUPABASE (two options):
#
# Option A — Supabase Dashboard (easiest for beginners):
#   Dashboard → Settings → Edge Functions → Add new secret
#   Add each key-value pair below.
#
# Option B — Supabase CLI:
#   supabase secrets set ONESIGNAL_APP_ID=your_value
#   supabase secrets set ONESIGNAL_REST_API_KEY=your_value
#
# SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY and SUPABASE_ANON_KEY are
# automatically available inside every Edge Function — you do NOT need
# to set them manually.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# OneSignal — get these from https://onesignal.com
# Dashboard → Your App → Settings → Keys & IDs
ONESIGNAL_APP_ID=your_onesignal_app_id_here
ONESIGNAL_REST_API_KEY=your_onesignal_rest_api_key_here

# AI Inference service — required by Phase 7 Edge Functions:
#   ai-predict-price, ai-bid-forecast, ai-retrain-trigger,
#   ai-model-promote, ai-model-rollback
#
# Set to the public base URL of your FastAPI service (no trailing slash).
# Examples:
#   http://your-server-ip:8000          (if self-hosted on a VPS)
#   https://ai.ecyamunara.rw            (if behind a reverse proxy / domain)
#
# Deploy with:
#   supabase secrets set AI_INFERENCE_URL=https://your-fastapi-url
AI_INFERENCE_URL=http://localhost:8000

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HOW TO GET YOUR ONESIGNAL KEYS (step by step):
#
# 1. Go to https://onesignal.com → Sign up free (no credit card)
# 2. Click "New App/Website"
# 3. Name: ecyamunara-rnp
# 4. Platform: Google Android (Mobile Push)
# 5. For Android setup, OneSignal will ask for a Firebase Server Key.
#    Since you are not using Firebase, use OneSignal's own Android setup:
#    → Choose "Use OneSignal's own configuration" if available
#    → OR: Create a free Firebase project ONLY for the messaging key
#      (Firebase Messaging is FREE on the Spark plan — no billing needed)
#      Firebase Console → Project Settings → Cloud Messaging → Server key
# 6. After setup, go to Settings → Keys & IDs
# 7. Copy "OneSignal App ID" → paste as ONESIGNAL_APP_ID
# 8. Copy "REST API Key"  → paste as ONESIGNAL_REST_API_KEY
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
